From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:08:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/char/serial: retry a pending byte after load when the
 backend can't be watched

serial_post_load() re-arms transmission of a byte that was in flight at
savevm time (tsr_retry > 0) by calling qemu_chr_fe_add_watch(). When the
chardev can't be watched at that moment -- a socket server chardev with no
client connected yet returns 0 -- no watch is installed, nothing ever calls
serial_xmit() again, and the transmitter stays busy forever: the guest sees
THRE/TEMT clear and its console is dead after the restore.

Schedule a one-shot bottom half in that case. serial_xmit() then either
sends the byte, installs a watch, or drops the byte after the retry limit,
which is what would have happened without the snapshot.

Reproducer: a guest printing steadily to a socket chardev whose client
stops reading; savevm while the socket is full; restart with -loadvm and
no client attached. Before: console silent forever (tsr_retry=1, lsr=0
after load). After: output resumes.
---
 hw/char/serial.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/char/serial.c b/hw/char/serial.c
index 0729cd2ce9d7b122d13bd6b08b8b74962fb86a2e..5a99918de512f7e4a57b7550a7669c4bc40ab25f 100644
--- a/hw/char/serial.c
+++ b/hw/char/serial.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #include "chardev/char-serial.h"
 #include "qapi/error.h"
 #include "qemu/timer.h"
+#include "qemu/main-loop.h"
 #include "system/reset.h"
 #include "system/runstate.h"
 #include "qemu/error-report.h"
@@ -646,6 +647,15 @@ static int serial_pre_load(void *opaque)
     return 0;
 }
 
+static void serial_retry_bh(void *opaque)
+{
+    SerialState *s = opaque;
+
+    if (s->tsr_retry > 0 && !s->watch_tag) {
+        serial_xmit(s);
+    }
+}
+
 static int serial_post_load(void *opaque, int version_id)
 {
     SerialState *s = opaque;
@@ -672,6 +682,16 @@ static int serial_post_load(void *opaque, int version_id)
         assert(s->watch_tag == 0);
         s->watch_tag = qemu_chr_fe_add_watch(&s->chr, G_IO_OUT | G_IO_HUP,
                                              serial_watch_cb, s);
+        if (!s->watch_tag) {
+            /*
+             * The backend can't be watched (e.g. a server socket with no
+             * client yet), so nothing would ever retry and the transmitter
+             * would stay busy forever. Retry once the load is done;
+             * serial_xmit() drops the byte if the backend still can't take it.
+             */
+            aio_bh_schedule_oneshot(qemu_get_aio_context(),
+                                    serial_retry_bh, s);
+        }
     } else {
         /* tsr_retry == 0 implies LSR.TEMT = 1 (transmitter empty).  */
         if (!(s->lsr & UART_LSR_TEMT)) {
